      "before_answer": "### Warranty Policy on Water or Flood Damage\nAccording to the documentation [Source 1] and [Source 4], the warranty policy does not cover damage caused by accident, abuse, misuse, flood, fire, earthquake, or other external causes. This explicitly excludes water or flood damage from the scope of coverage.\n\n### Next Steps\nIf you have experienced water or flood damage to your device, I recommend exploring other support options. You can contact our support team directly via phone at **1800-123-NEXORA** or through the support portal at **www.nexoraelectronics.com/support** for further assistance. \n\nWould you like to:\n1. **Contact Support** directly for personalized advice.\n2. **Explore FAQs** for more information on device care and maintenance.\n3. **Check Warranty Status** for your specific device (I can do this proactively for your Nexora Thermostat Pro or LumiGlow Smart Light).",
      "after_answer": "### Warranty Policy on Water or Flood Damage\nAccording to the documentation [Source 1] and [Source 3], the warranty policy explicitly excludes coverage for water damage and flood damage. This is stated under the exclusions from coverage section [Source 4], which mentions that damage caused by accident, abuse, misuse, flood, fire, earthquake, or other external causes is not covered.\n\nTherefore, if your device has been damaged by water or flood, the warranty will not apply. \n\nThe logical next action would be to consider options for repair or replacement outside of the warranty, or to contact our support team to discuss possible alternatives. Would you like me to **create a support ticket** for further assistance?"
